// Chapter 1: The Grind. What happens after each event, in Steven's order (the old game's Play.cs queue): the final
// table, the Classic's days, the first title, the first cooler or bust, going broke, then the goal.

title: BeforeEvent
---
// week two (CH1_WEEKS.md): the first live game you start on or after Monday 19 January. Live only: it's in the room.
<<if $chapter == 1 and not $online and $day >= 14 and not $wk2>>
    <<set $wk2 to true>>
    <<film c1_w2>>
    I ran your bubble hands through my solver last night. #card
    -> "Does it fold for you too?"
        <<film c1_w2_a>>
    -> Say nothing.
        <<film c1_w2_b>>
    <<film c1_w2b>>
<<endif>>
===

title: AfterEvent
---
// the final table, if you met someone there (ft_won_tommy, ft_lost_tommy)
<<if $ft_end != "">>
    <<film {$ft_end}>>
<<endif>>
// the first tournament ends the prologue: Monday, and the job decision at home
<<if $event == "local">>
    <<jump Monday>>
<<endif>>
<<if $event == "classic" and $qualified>>
    <<film classic_day1>>
    <<clock "11:58 PM">>
    Slick: Day 2. Go to sleep. Don't celebrate yet. #text
<<endif>>
<<if $event == "classic2">>
    <<if $won>>
        <<film trentbeat>>
    <<else>>
        <<film {$classic_end}>>
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
<<if $won and not $firstwin_seen>>
    <<set $firstwin_seen to true>>
    <<if $online>>
        // an online first title: no photo, no trophy, no locker (TABLE.md §11)
        Slick: Saw the screenshot. Your name at the top of the lobby. Proud of you, kid. #text
        Slick: Left something for you at the Lucky Seven. Every champion needs a pair. #text
        Inside: a pair of pixelated sunglasses and a note. “Deal with it.”
    <<else>>
        <<film firstwin>>
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
<<if $cooler and not $badbeat_seen>>
    <<set $badbeat_seen to true>>
    <<film badbeat>>
    <<clock "2:16 AM">>
    Mustich: Heard you got coolered. Brutal. Maybe this game just isn't for everyone. #text
    <<film badbeat2>>
<<elseif $bust and not $lesson_seen>>
    <<set $lesson_seen to true>>
    <<film lesson1>>
<<endif>>
<<if $chapter == 1 and $bankroll < 55>>
    <<detour Broke>>
<<endif>>
// week three at the diner: the first night after Friday 30 January's texts that you've played a live event
<<if $chapter == 1 and not $online and $wk3 and not $wk3d and not $classic_done>>
    <<set $wk3d to true>>
    <<if $job == "nights">>
        <<film c1_w3_diner_keep>>
    <<else>>
        <<film c1_w3_diner_quit>>
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
<<if $chapter == 2>>
    <<detour C2AfterEvent>>
<<endif>>
<<detour CheckGoal>>
===

title: AfterSleep
---
// week three: Friday 30 January, with the pay and the rent. Texts read anywhere.
<<if $chapter == 1 and $day >= 25 and not $wk3 and not $classic_done>>
    <<set $wk3 to true>>
    <<clock "8:05 AM">>
    <<if $job == "nights">>
        Friday. The pay lands. $600 leaves the same morning for the apartment.
    <<else>>
        Friday. $600 leaves the same morning for the apartment.
    <<endif>>
    Slick: Rent's in. Good. Look at what's left, not at what you won. #text
    <<if $debt > 0>>
        Slick: You still owe me {$debt_s}. Half of every profit comes back to me until it's gone. That's not interest. That's the lesson. #text
    <<else>>
        Slick: You owe me nothing now. Which means every dollar you lose from here is yours. Notice how that feels. #text
    <<endif>>
    <<if $job == "nights">>
        Lou: Henderson deck, Monday, 9. Nobody gets the weekend off for "a hobby." #text
        David: you look tired in that photo. quit the deck. or dont. but sleep #text
    <<else>>
        David: rent day!!! how are we feeling. be honest. honest = fine. dishonest = I bring soup #text
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
// Classic week: the first night on or after Monday 9 February, at the diner
<<if $chapter == 1 and $day >= 35 and not $wk4a and not $classic_done>>
    <<set $wk4a to true>>
    <<film c1_w4_diner>>
<<endif>>
// the night before: Friday 13 February (or the morning of, if the calendar jumped past it)
<<if $chapter == 1 and $day >= 39 and not $wk4b and not $classic_done>>
    <<set $wk4b to true>>
    <<film c1_w4_eve>>
    <<clock "11:34 PM">>
    Slick: Early night. No new hands tonight, only the ones you've already missed. Review them. Then sleep. #text
    David: TOMORROW!!! I'll be on my couch screaming at a stream of nothing. Fold the junk. I'm so proud I could scream. I'm screaming. #text
    <<if $job == "nights">>
        Lou: Henderson numbers, Monday, 9. Good luck with your "event." #text
    <<endif>>
    <<film c1_w4_eve2>>
<<endif>>
// the night can end the chapter (the Classic's day gone by) or cross the milestone (a paycheck)
<<if $chapter == 2>>
    <<detour C2AfterSleep>>
<<endif>>
<<detour CheckGoal>>
===

title: CheckGoal
---
<<if $chapter == 2>>
    <<detour C2CheckGoal>>
<<endif>>
// Test Beta 1.1: Chapter 1 ends when the Biscayne Classic is over for you (out on Day 1, Day 2 played, or the day gone).
// $5,000 before it is a milestone, with one text from Slick.
<<if $chapter == 1 and $peak >= 5000 and not $stake_seen>>
    <<set $stake_seen to true>>
    Slick: Now you're not playing scared. #text
<<endif>>
<<if $chapter == 1 and $classic_done>>
    <<jump ChapterEnd>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Broke
---
// rock bottom at the Lucky Seven: Slick's way out depends on the job (old broke / broke_n)
<<film broke>>
<<if $job == "nights">>
    <<film broke_n>>
<<else>>
    <<film broke_q>>
<<endif>>
Rock bottom #card
$1,000 now. Half your profits go back to Slick until it's repaid. #hint
CF Tilt's Comeback Freeroll is open to you while your roll is low. #hint
-> Take Slick's stake
    <<stake 1000>>
    <<film broke_stake>>
-> Grind the freerolls
    <<film broke_free>>
-> Ask Lou for the job back <<if $job == "quit">>
    Lou laughs for a full ten seconds. "Your job? We gave it to the intern." That night Slick sends $500: "Make it last."
    <<money 500 "From Slick, after Lou said no">>
===

title: ChapterEnd
---
// with the day job, David texts first at ten thousand (old david1); then Slick sends you to the Circuit
<<if $job == "nights" and $peak >= 10000 and not $david_seen>>
    <<set $david_seen to true>>
    <<clock "6:02 PM">>
    David: TEN THOUSAND?? FROM POKER?? AND YOU STILL WENT TO WORK TODAY??? #text
    David: im just saying. lou doesnt deserve you. the felt does #text
<<endif>>
<<set $chapter to 2>>
<<clock "1:13 AM">>
Slick: You've outgrown Biscayne. The Circuit stops at Silver Strike every couple of months. Every event gives a ring. Check the calendar. #text
// Chapter 2 (Milestone B): Tommy drives you north to the first stop (storyboards until they're filmed)
<<film c2_drive>>
<<film c2>>
===
